KZ3 patch 2142 (RSX pass 133): a texture level that does not fit in the 64 MB upload ring submits the command list first instead of being skipped.
Design and code from the Killzone 2 port (Project Pyrrhus, its patch 6048); both projects are MIT and have the same owner.

Symptom (Killzone 2): the first-level sky came out green. create_texture_mipped staged each level in the per-frame
upload ring (UPLOAD_SIZE) and, when a level did not fit in what was left, hit "break": no copy was recorded, the new D3D12
resource kept its initial zeros, the cache entry still pointed at it and the guest bytes' hash never changed, so it was never
uploaded again. create_texture_cube and create_texture_3d returned NULL on the same check (white for good).
Killzone 3 has the same three checks (rsx_live_draw.c, create_texture_mipped / _cube / _3d); not seen as a symptom in KZ3 yet.

Fix: libs/video/rsx_upload_ring.h (pure C, host test tools/smoke/test_upload_ring.sh) decides fit / submit first / too big;
ld_upload_take submits the list (new flush reason LD_FLUSH_UPLOAD_RING, "upring" in [perf-flush]) and stages at 0, as
ld_gv_upload_rows and the retire queue already do; a flush invalidates the state memo. One [tex-upload] line per submit
(first 32, then every 256th) names the guest texture; a level larger than the whole ring is still not uploaded but is now
reported. Upstream candidate (the check is in ps3recomp's live draw).

